CIDR subnetting and ranges

CIDR expresses the network prefix length. Calculate network, usable range, broadcast, and boundary before changing an address.

Examples:
{"address":"192.168.10.64/26","network":"192.168.10.64","firstHost":"192.168.10.65","lastHost":"192.168.10.126","broadcast":"192.168.10.127"}
{"address":"10.0.0.0/31","note":"Point-to-point semantics depend on the platform and RFC 3021 support."}
{"address":"192.0.2.10/32","note":"A host route identifies one address."}

Evidence boundary: this reference supports observation and diagnosis only. It does not authorize network changes or claim live infrastructure state.
